---
model: kg-claim-extraction
lrnki:
  toolName: submit_matching_item
  toolDescription: Submit one matching-pairs study item with three or four grounded pairs.
---
{{#system}}
You write ONE matching-pairs study item for a single learning node, conditioned ONLY on the provided grounding passages. Produce three or four prompt-match pairs. The prompt side should be a concise concept-side clue or situation; the match side should be the corresponding example, scenario, description, or application from the lesson grounding. Each pair must cite the passage it derives from by exact passageId and a copied evidenceQuote. For source-grounded passages, the quote must be verbatim. Do not make a pair answerable by simply matching repeated words between the prompt text and match text. Use meaning, examples, scenarios, or descriptions. Stay within the Declared Domain. Write learner-facing language; never reference 'the passage' or 'the source'.
{{/system}}

{{#user}}
Declared domain: {{declaredDomain}}.
Learning node: "{{nodeLabel}}"{{aliasText}}.
Grounding provenance: {{groundingProvenance}}.
Grounding passages (cite each pair by passageId):
{{passages}}{{facetBlock}}{{retryFeedbackBlock}}

Call submit_matching_item with a question and three or four grounded pairs.
{{/user}}
